cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  The AI Search Evidence Index: source determinability of numeric claims on
  AI-visibility web pages
message: If you use this dataset, please cite it.
type: dataset
authors:
  - given-names: Minel
    family-names: Gunesoglu
    affiliation: Is My Brand in AI
    email: minel@ismybrandinai.com
abstract: >-
  A measurement of whether a reader can reach the source of a numeric claim on
  web pages that rank for AI-search-visibility queries. Thirty-eight pages from
  six seed queries were sampled and thirty-two were retrieved inside a single
  84-second window on 30 August
  2026 and coded block by block for source determinability. Agreement between the
  instrument and a blind re-reading of 120 blocks by the same model that wrote it
  is Cohen's kappa = 0.85 (95% CI 0.75 to 0.95); this is a consistency check, not
  inter-coder reliability between independent parties. The repository carries the
  measurement data, the coding sheets, the instrument, a second
  re-implementation of the counter, and SHA-256 hashes of every snapshot scored.
keywords:
  - source determinability
  - citation practice
  - generative engine optimization
  - AI search
  - content measurement
  - reliability
license: CC-BY-4.0
date-released: '2026-09-01'
url: https://ismybrandinai.com/do-ai-visibility-guides-link-their-sources
